jo: Quick note — the new Next + LangChain starter (examples/next-langchain-stub) is confusing some users. Intermittent 401s on server-side embed calls when running with CONCURRENT=3.

priya: Is the starter using the JS SDK or a raw fetch impl?

jo: We kept raw fetch to minimize deps. Server handler looks like:
```js
export default async (req, res) => {
  const resp = await fetch(`${process.env.RW_API_URL}/v1/embeddings`, {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.RW_API_KEY}` },
    body: JSON.stringify({ input: req.body.text }),
  });
  if (!resp.ok) return res.status(resp.status).send(await resp.text());
  res.json(await resp.json());
};
```

ben: That bypasses the SDK's refresh/retry/circuit-breaker behavior. When KMS rotates keys or local runs are bursty, folks hit transient 401s and confusing errors.

priya: Recommend switching server handlers to the SDK by default and making RAW_FETCH an opt-in env var. Also add a short note in README about SSR/cold-start/auth caveats.

jo: Filed issue + small PR to swap to sdkClient.embed by default, add REDWOOD_SAMPLE_RAW_FETCH env flag (defaults to false), and include a CI test that returns 401 then 200 to simulate rotation.

doc-bot: Created issue https://github.com/redwood-inference/next-langchain-stub/issues/1 and PR https://github.com/redwood-inference/next-langchain-stub/pull/2

ben: Also add a one-liner Promise.all test in examples/tests to exercise concurrent SSR so the harness catches regressions. And add telemetry tags: stage=embed, outcome=401|ok for better triage.

priya: Long-term: we should align retry semantics across SDKs (which status codes trigger refresh, max attempts, backoff). I'll kick off a short RFC with SDK maintainers.

ci: CI started for branch jo/sdk-default (job 7123).

jo: Thanks — merging after green. I'll monitor Console for auth spikes and close the issue after 48h if stable.
